data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"A sequence with `n` tokens needs `ceil(n / block_size)` blocks, and token `p` (0-based) lives in\ntable index `p // block_size` at offset `p % block_size`. A token starts a new block exactly when\n`p % block_size == 0`. For reuse, keep the free ids in a min-heap so that the lowest id is always\ntaken first. Check the free count before you take anything, so a failed request changes nothing."},"hints_note":null}

